body:
@jlovejoy In regards to usage, I have noted it is fairly new. So far 8 publicly available projects use it + the 82 teams that signed up for the HeroX challenge I made may use it. I do hope to quality for an identifier though, because lots of cloud software that Stark Drones has as open source may by able to use the short identifier in the configs.
In regards to blocking somebody, he has replied on multiple pull requests I have had on multiple places. Most of these pull requests in the general guidelines state that a pull request isn't the place for staying disagreement but rather open mailing list. I feel like it was a given I didn't want to continue the discussion in the actual pull request and I don't have hours of my time reply to the same guy back and forth.
I am generally okay with people stating disagreement, if it is with respect to my time and not done in a passive aggressive way. Pull requests are not the appropriate venue for that.
